{%- comment -%}
  Structured data for the product page: Product, FAQPage and BreadcrumbList.

  Both the FAQPage and the Product node come from the catalogue upload when it
  supplied them, and are built here from live data when it did not.

  custom.product_schema is the SEO-written Product node, imported by
  scripts/import-product-schema.py, which repairs it on the way in: the stored
  copy had a null price on 1,015 of 1,308 rows, so 996 were filled from the
  sheet's price column and the 19 with no price anywhere had their offers
  block dropped rather than emitted broken. sku, gtin and @id are injected
  there too, since the stored copy omits them.

  It declares AED and thefragrancesecrets.com URLs, which are correct for the
  live store. On any other store — a dev or preview copy — those will not match
  the page, so the fallback below is what should be used there.

  One thing the stored node cannot carry is aggregateRating, which depends on
  live review counts. The fallback still emits it. Once reviews exist on live,
  that has to be merged in at render time or the stars are lost.

  Usage: {% render 'product-schema', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign currency = cart.currency.iso_code | default: shop.currency
  assign product_url = shop.url | append: product.url
  assign description = product.description | strip_html | strip | truncate: 900

  assign rating_value = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating
  assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | plus: 0

  assign ship_rate = settings.shipping_flat_rate | default: 8 | times: 1
  assign ship_days_min = settings.delivery_days_min | default: 1 | times: 1
  assign ship_days_max = settings.delivery_days_max | default: 4 | times: 1

  assign title_check = product.title | downcase
  assign gender = ''
  if title_check contains 'unisex'
    assign gender = 'unisex'
  elsif title_check contains 'for women' or title_check contains "women's"
    assign gender = 'female'
  elsif title_check contains 'for men' or title_check contains "men's"
    assign gender = 'male'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  shippingDetails, built once and appended to every offers block below —
  there are four of them (stored and fallback, each single-price and
  multi-price) and a shipping block written out four times is a block that
  will disagree with itself.

  Why it is worth having: without it Google shows no delivery information in
  a product rich result, and a listing that says nothing about shipping loses
  to one beside it that says "free delivery". The figures come from the same
  settings the PDP quotes, so the page, the structured data and checkout
  cannot drift.

  Emitted as one rate — the paid one — rather than two. Schema.org has no
  property for "free above a threshold": expressing it needs a second
  OfferShippingDetails whose rate is 0, and nothing in that second entry can
  carry the condition, so it would read as unconditional free delivery on
  every order. Understating by one flat rate is a small cost; a free-delivery
  badge the checkout then contradicts is the bait-and-switch pattern the CCPA
  guidelines name, and it gets items disapproved in Merchant Center.

  handlingTime is 0–1 days because an order placed before the cutoff ships
  the same day and one after it the next; transitTime is the delivery window
  from the same settings the PDP's arrival date uses.

  Deliberately no hasMerchantReturnPolicy. This store accepts returns only
  for damaged, defective, incorrect or incomplete orders — faults, which are
  a statutory right rather than a returns window. The only way to say that in
  schema.org is MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow with merchantReturnDays,
  which Google surfaces as a plain "2-day returns", and that promises a
  change-of-mind window the store does not offer. Omitted on purpose; add it
  if and only if the refund policy itself changes.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture offer_shipping -%}
,"shippingDetails":{"@type":"OfferShippingDetails","shippingRate":{"@type":"MonetaryAmount","value":{{ ship_rate | json }},"currency":{{ currency | json }}},"shippingDestination":{"@type":"DefinedRegion","addressCountry":"AE"},"deliveryTime":{"@type":"ShippingDeliveryTime","handlingTime":{"@type":"QuantitativeValue","minValue":0,"maxValue":1,"unitCode":"DAY"},"transitTime":{"@type":"QuantitativeValue","minValue":{{ ship_days_min | json }},"maxValue":{{ ship_days_max | json }},"unitCode":"DAY"}}}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign offer_shipping = offer_shipping | strip -%}

{%- assign stored_product = product.metafields.custom.product_schema.value | default: product.metafields.custom.product_schema -%}
{%- if stored_product != blank -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The stored node supplies the written content — description, brand,
    category, audience, images — and nothing that moves. offers and
    aggregateRating are appended here from live data instead, because a
    snapshot cannot track them: when this was measured, 249 products still
    claimed InStock while sold out and 3 carried a stale price, which is what
    gets items disapproved in Merchant Center. scripts/strip-schema-offers.py
    removed both keys from the stored copy so this is the only source.

    remove_last on the closing brace lets the live keys be appended without
    parsing the JSON in Liquid. It is safe because the stored value is
    machine-generated, minified, and verified to end with "}" — the strip
    script refuses to write anything that does not.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign schema_base = stored_product | strip | remove_last: '}' -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ schema_base }}
{%- if rating_count > 0 and rating_value != blank -%}
,"aggregateRating":{"@type":"AggregateRating","ratingValue":{{ rating_value | json }},"reviewCount":{{ rating_count | json }}}
{%- endif -%}
{%- if product.price > 0 -%}
  {%- if product.price_min != product.price_max -%}
,"offers":{"@type":"AggregateOffer","offerCount":{{ product.variants.size }},"lowPrice":{{ product.price_min | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},"highPrice":{{ product.price_max | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},"priceCurrency":{{ currency | json }},"availability":{% if product.available %}"https://schema.org/InStock"{% else %}"https://schema.org/OutOfStock"{% endif %},"url":{{ product_url | json }},"seller":{"@type":"Organization","name":{{ shop.name | json }}}{{ offer_shipping }}}
  {%- else -%}
,"offers":{"@type":"Offer","url":{{ product_url | json }},"priceCurrency":{{ currency | json }},"price":{{ variant.price | default: product.price | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},"availability":{% if product.available %}"https://schema.org/InStock"{% else %}"https://schema.org/OutOfStock"{% endif %},"itemCondition":"https://schema.org/NewCondition","seller":{"@type":"Organization","name":{{ shop.name | json }}}{{ offer_shipping }}}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
}</script>
{%- else -%}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org/",
  "@type": "Product",
  "@id": {{ product_url | append: '#product' | json }},
  "name": {{ product.title | json }},
  "url": {{ product_url | json }},
  {%- if description != blank %}
  "description": {{ description | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  "brand": { "@type": "Brand", "name": {{ product.vendor | default: shop.name | json }} },
  {%- if product.type != blank %}
  "category": {{ product.type | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if gender != blank %}
  "audience": { "@type": "PeopleAudience", "suggestedGender": {{ gender | json }} },
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if variant.sku != blank %}
  "sku": {{ variant.sku | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if variant.barcode != blank %}
  "gtin": {{ variant.barcode | json }},
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if product.images.size > 0 %}
  "image": [
    {%- for image in product.images limit: 5 -%}
      {%- assign src = image | image_url: width: 1600 | split: '//' | last | prepend: 'https://' -%}
      {{ src | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ],
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if rating_count > 0 and rating_value != blank %}
  "aggregateRating": {
    "@type": "AggregateRating",
    "ratingValue": {{ rating_value | json }},
    "reviewCount": {{ rating_count | json }}
  },
  {%- endif %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Offers are emitted only with a real price, because a zero or null price
    makes the rich result invalid. Since the catalogue import that is now
    1,289 of 1,308 products; the remaining 19 carry no price in the source
    sheet and so ship without an offers block rather than with a broken one.

    priceCurrency follows the store, not a hardcoded value, so it corrects
    itself the moment the shop currency is switched to AED.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if product.price > 0 %}
    {%- if product.price_min != product.price_max %}
  "offers": {
    "@type": "AggregateOffer",
    "offerCount": {{ product.variants.size }},
    "lowPrice": {{ product.price_min | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},
    "highPrice": {{ product.price_max | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},
    "priceCurrency": {{ currency | json }},
    "availability": {% if product.available %}"https://schema.org/InStock"{% else %}"https://schema.org/OutOfStock"{% endif %},
    "url": {{ product_url | json }},
    "seller": { "@type": "Organization", "name": {{ shop.name | json }} }
    {{- offer_shipping -}}
  },
    {%- else %}
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "url": {{ product_url | json }},
    "priceCurrency": {{ currency | json }},
    "price": {{ variant.price | default: product.price | divided_by: 100.0 | json }},
    "availability": {% if product.available %}"https://schema.org/InStock"{% else %}"https://schema.org/OutOfStock"{% endif %},
    "itemCondition": "https://schema.org/NewCondition",
    "seller": { "@type": "Organization", "name": {{ shop.name | json }} }
    {{- offer_shipping -}}
  },
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endif %}
  "isPartOf": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#website' | json }} }
}
</script>

{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} FAQ: the uploaded schema when present, otherwise built from the same metafield the page renders {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign faq_schema = product.metafields.custom.faq_schema.value | default: product.metafields.custom.faq_schema -%}
{%- if faq_schema != blank -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ faq_schema }}</script>
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign faq_text = product.metafields.custom.faq.value | default: product.metafields.custom.faq -%}
  {%- if faq_text != blank -%}
    {%- assign faq_lines = faq_text | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
    {%- assign pair_count = 0 -%}
    {%- for line in faq_lines -%}
      {%- assign qa = line | split: ' :: ' -%}
      {%- if qa.size >= 2 -%}{%- assign pair_count = pair_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if pair_count > 0 -%}
      <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org/",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {%- assign written = 0 -%}
          {%- for line in faq_lines -%}
            {%- assign qa = line | split: ' :: ' -%}
            {%- if qa.size >= 2 -%}
              {%- assign written = written | plus: 1 -%}
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": {{ qa[0] | strip | json }},
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ qa[1] | strip | json }} }
              }{%- unless written == pair_count -%},{%- endunless -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        ]
      }
      </script>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "@id": {{ product_url | append: '#breadcrumb' | json }},
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": {{ shop.url | append: '/' | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Perfumes", "item": {{ shop.url | append: '/collections/all' | json }} },
    {%- if collection.title != blank and collection.url != blank %}
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": {{ collection.title | json }}, "item": {{ shop.url | append: collection.url | json }} },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "name": {{ product.title | json }}, "item": {{ product_url | json }} }
    {%- else %}
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": {{ product.title | json }}, "item": {{ product_url | json }} }
    {%- endif %}
  ]
}
</script>
